firefox 152 on DragonFly -- build orchestration not yet folded into the overlay
=============================================================================

The dragonfly/ patches (auto-applied in the patch phase) cover all *source*
fixes. The steps below are the build/runtime orchestration that still has to be
supplied by hand until it is baked into the port. With them, firefox 152 builds
and runs on Wayland (firefox --version -> Mozilla Firefox 152.0).

1. Compiler
   USE_GCC_VERSION=13 selects gcc13 for the main compile (set in overlay.dops).
   Additionally pass on the make command line, because a few host-tool/link
   steps otherwise fall back to base cc:
       CC=/usr/local/bin/gcc13 CXX=/usr/local/bin/g++13 CPP=/usr/local/bin/cpp13
   clang (llvm19) stays in use for bindgen and the wasm sandbox via
   --with-clang-path and BINARY_ALIAS.

2. bindgen C++ header shim (REQUIRED, else libclang fails on <version>/<bit>)
   clang's default C++ stdlib is base gcc 8.3's libstdc++ (no C++20 headers);
   pointing clang at gcc13's headers alone conflicts with DragonFly libc over
   C-function exception specs. Build a shim once:
       SHIM=${WRKDIR}/ff-cxx13
       cp -a /usr/local/lib/gcc13/include/c++/* $SHIM/
       for h in cstdlib cwchar cstdio cwctype; do
         sed -i '' -e 's/throw ()//g' -e 's/_GLIBCXX_NOTHROW//g' $SHIM/$h
       done
   Then inject into the generated BINDGEN_SYSTEM_FLAGS (config.statusd/substs +
   config/autoconf.mk), removing buildconfig.rs to force regeneration:
       -nostdinc++ -isystem $SHIM -isystem $SHIM/x86_64-portbld-dragonfly6.5 \
       -isystem $SHIM/backward
   (BINDGEN_CFLAGS env at configure time is the intended hook, but the compat
   port passes it as a make var which firefox's configure does not read from the
   environment -- fix that and step 2's injection becomes a one-liner.)

3. wasm2c host tool (RLBox wasm sandbox)
   dist/host/bin/wasm2c is built with gcc13 (needs GLIBCXX_3.4.31) but the ld
   hints resolve libstdc++.so.6 to gcc11's first. Wrap it:
       mv dist/host/bin/wasm2c{,.real}
       printf '#!/bin/sh\nexport LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/usr/local/lib/gcc13:$LD_LIBRARY_PATH\nexec %s "$@"\n' \
         .../wasm2c.real > dist/host/bin/wasm2c && chmod +x it
   Run the whole build with LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/usr/local/lib/gcc13:/usr/local/lib.

4. Installed launcher
   libxul rpath is /usr/local/lib, but firefox's own libmozgtk.so /
   libmozwayland.so live in /usr/local/lib/firefox, and the runtime needs
   gcc13's libstdc++. Replace the /usr/local/bin/firefox symlink with:
       #!/bin/sh
       export LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/usr/local/lib/firefox:/usr/local/lib/gcc13:${LD_LIBRARY_PATH}
       export MOZ_ENABLE_WAYLAND=1
       exec /usr/local/lib/firefox/firefox "$@"
   Proper fix: add -Wl,-rpath=/usr/local/lib/firefox and .../gcc13 to the link.

5. Parallelism
   MAKE_JOBS_NUMBER=12 (32 parallel gcc13 C++ jobs OOM on 32 GB).

Wayland: the session must export WAYLAND_DISPLAY (see start-gnome.sh's
dbus-update-activation-environment); MOZ_ENABLE_WAYLAND=1 is set by the launcher.
